uses of resources 



✅ get
📌 Purpose: Single resource ya list me se ek resource ka detail dekhna
📦 Example:

kubectl get pod pod-name
kubectl describe pod pod-name

✅ list
📌 Purpose: Ek type ke saare resources ki list lana
📦 Example:


kubectl get pods         # sab pods ka list

✅ watch
📌 Purpose: Kisi resource me live change dekhna (continuous stream)
📦 Example:


kubectl get pods -w       # live dekhne ke liye jab pods create/delete ho rahe

✅ create
📌 Purpose: Naya resource banana
📦 Example:


kubectl run pod-name nginx --image=nginx
kubectl apply -f pod.yaml   

✅ delete
📌 Purpose: Resource delete karna
📦 Example:


kubectl delete pod my-pod
kubectl delete -f service.yaml

✅ patch
📌 Purpose: Resource me chhoti si update karna bina puri YAML file diye
📦 Example:

kubectl patch pod my-test-pod -p '{"metadata":{"annotations":{"patched-by":"faisal"}}}'
⚠️ patch mainly JSON format me chhoti update ke liye hota hai

✅ update
📌 Purpose: Pura resource update karna (replace karna)
📦 Example:

kubectl replace -f pod.yaml
